{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789240285,"nonce":"FbvmyMqVhMimV2U2NLIfrftTatQ=","title":"Per-call overheads in the interpreter loop and the JIT dispatch helpers","message":"Profiles of bench/delta_blue.wren (steady state, 2000 outer iterations) and a 4M-call micro-benchmark (interpreter):\n\n- The interpreter registered the live register file with a thread-local guard on every loop iteration, rewrote the JIT context through a thread-local lookup each iteration, cloned the callee's MIR Arc just to check for an AOT stub, and the module cache keyed on one Rc pointer missed on every call/return because a module-level frame and a method frame hold different Rcs of the same name.\n- In compiled code, trace gates (WLIFT_TRACE_JIT_IC, TRACE_NONLEAF, TRACE_NATIVE_ENTRY, TRACE_STALE_SUBSCRIPT) called getenv on every dispatch: __findenv_locked showed at 6% of steady-state samples.\n- wren_known_call_nocheck_inner made about a dozen thread-local accesses per call (context, depth, roots); on macOS each is an out-of-line _tlv_get_addr, the top symbol at 27% of samples.\n\nFixes: guard registered once per run loop; context written through a raw pointer fetched once; four-entry module cache; trace gates cached in OnceLock; the three JIT thread-locals merged into one JitThread struct fetched once per helper (jit_state()).\n\nMeasurements (CPU): 4M-call interpreter micro 900 -\u003e 310 ms (wren_cli 108 ms); delta_blue interpreter 640 -\u003e 380 ms (wren_cli 100 ms); delta_blue x400 tiered 1.05 -\u003e 0.85 s (wren_cli 1.06 s). Remaining interpreter call cost is structural: two loop prologues per call (call and return), frame push/pop, register-file fill, argument SmallVec; the JIT's generic dispatch (wren_call_N -\u003e dispatch_call -\u003e dispatch_method) still dominates polymorphic sites and needs a polymorphic inline cache.","files":null}]}